%S A401547 12,18,19,22,23,32,41,42,43,48,52,56,61,67,70,71,72,74,75,76,78,79,84,
%T A401547 88,89,93,96,98,99,106,107,112,113,114,115,117,118,119,128,132,133,
%U A401547 136,139,140,142,143,146,147,149,150,151,155,156,157,158,159,162,163
%N A401547 Numbers k such that the greedy algorithm for writing k as a sum of positive squares uses more squares than necessary; i.e., numbers k such that A053610(k) > A002828(k).
%C A401547 Positions of nonzero terms in A062535.
%C A401547 The greedy algorithm repeatedly subtracts the largest square not exceeding the remainder; A053610(k) is the number of steps. By Lagrange's theorem the minimum number of squares A002828(k) is at most 4.
%C A401547 This sequence has natural density 1: among k <= 10^4, 10^5, 10^6, 10^7, 10^8 the proportion of k not in this sequence is 0.356, 0.264, 0.202, 0.155, 0.120 respectively. It can be proved that the number of k <= N not in this sequence is at most 10.3*N^(15/16).
%H A401547 Abo Khmiss, <a href="/A401547/b401547.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%e A401547 12 is a term: greedy gives 12 = 9 + 1 + 1 + 1 (4 squares) but 12 = 4 + 4 + 4 (3 squares).
%e A401547 23 is a term: greedy gives 23 = 16 + 4 + 1 + 1 + 1 (5 squares) but 23 = 9 + 9 + 4 + 1 (4 squares).
%e A401547 13 is not a term: greedy gives 13 = 9 + 4, which is minimal.
%o A401547 (Python)
%o A401547 from math import isqrt
%o A401547 def greedy(n):
%o A401547     c = 0
%o A401547     while n: n -= isqrt(n)**2; c += 1
%o A401547     return c
%o A401547 def least(n):
%o A401547     if isqrt(n)**2 == n: return 1
%o A401547     a = 0
%o A401547     while 2*a*a <= n:
%o A401547         if isqrt(n-a*a)**2 == n-a*a: return 2
%o A401547         a += 1
%o A401547     while n % 4 == 0: n //= 4
%o A401547     return 4 if n % 8 == 7 else 3
%o A401547 print([k for k in range(1, 200) if greedy(k) > least(k)])
%Y A401547 Cf. A053610, A002828, A062535, A006892, A004215.
%K A401547 nonn,easy,new
%O A401547 1,1
